  "articleBody": "Choosing the right handrail for your outdoor stairs isn't just about aesthetics; it's about safety, durability, and a comfortable user experience. When making your selection, you'll want to prioritize secure construction. Look for materials and designs that can be firmly anchored and provide reliable support. Weather-resistant materials are crucial for outdoor handrails, especially in an area like Denver where we experience varied conditions. Materials that can withstand rain, snow, and freeze-thaw cycles without corroding or deteriorating are ideal. A comfortable grip size is also really important. The handrail should be easy for all users to grasp securely, not too thick or too thin. Consider its compatibility with your existing structure; will it blend well, and can it be safely mounted? Finally, always choose a design that truly supports the intended user, rather than just meeting minimum appearance standards. This means thinking about continuity, height, and how it aligns with the steps or ramp. If you're unsure about specific materials or code requirements, a professional installer can guide you to the best choice for your particular needs and ensure it's installed correctly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
